# Normalise line endings at commit time, and check out LF everywhere.
#
# WHY `eol=lf` AND NOT THE WINDOWS DEFAULT: this repository is developed on
# Windows, but its toolchain is not Windows-flavoured. `rustfmt`, `cargo`,
# Vite and pnpm all emit LF; without this file Git rewrites those files to
# CRLF on checkout and every subsequent diff shows whole files as changed,
# which makes review useless and hides real edits.
#
# The Windows application manifest is the concrete reason this matters here.
# It is embedded byte-for-byte into the executable by the resource compiler,
# and a malformed manifest makes the binary refuse to start with
# `os error 14001` -- a failure that `cargo build` reports as success.
# See `src-tauri/windows-app-manifest.xml`. Leaving its encoding to a
# platform default is exactly the class of mistake that already cost a
# debugging session on 2 September 2026.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these, never try to diff them as text.
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.jpg   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# Lockfiles are generated. Keep them in the repository (reproducible builds)
# but collapse them in diffs so review stays readable.
pnpm-lock.yaml      linguist-generated=true -diff
src-tauri/Cargo.lock linguist-generated=true -diff
